# VITAL OS — environment template
# Copy to .env.local and fill in real values. Never commit .env.local.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local          (macOS / Linux)
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env.local   (Windows PowerShell)
#
# Next.js only reads this file at startup — restart `npm run dev` after edits.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required — Google Gemini
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Clinical reasoning, intent parsing, and the /api/vital assistant.
# Key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Model IDs, both defaulting to gemini-3.5-flash when unset.
# GEMINI_CLINICAL_MODEL — intent parsing and clinical reasoning
# GEMINI_MODEL          — the /api/vital general assistant
# Google retires flash models on a rolling schedule; these are env vars so a
# deprecation is a config change, not a code change.
# GEMINI_CLINICAL_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required — Supabase
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The patient roster lives in Postgres. Without these the roster, chart views,
# and every AI turn that reads patient data will fail.
# Values: Supabase dashboard -> Settings -> API
#
# Use the `anon` / `public` key. Do NOT use the service_role key here — the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix ships this value to every browser that loads the app.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# When set, Groq becomes the primary leg for transcription and intent parsing,
# with Gemini as the fallback if Groq exceeds its 2500 ms latency budget.
# Leave blank to run Gemini-only; the provider chain skips unconfigured legs.
# Key: https://console.groq.com/keys
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_INTENT_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# GROQ_WHISPER_MODEL=whisper-large-v3-turbo
